! Changelog

|!Version |!Date |!Changes |
|0.1.30 |2026-05-18 |Phase 0 of suite-wide consolidation: new `file-ops.js` library module exporting `cleanEmptyDirs`, `deleteGenerated`, `renameGenerated`, `deleteDerived`, `renameDerived` — the helpers currently inlined verbatim in `routes/delete.js` and `routes/rename.js` (and partially copied with a nested-dir bug into `file-pipeline/finalize-route.js`). Additive only; the existing route handlers continue to use their inline copies until Phase 1. New `test/test-file-ops.js` exercises all five exports against a per-spec temp directory, including the nested `_derived/_derived/` case that finalize-route's old `cleanupDerived()` fails on |
|0.1.29 |2026-05-17 |Test coverage push: 8 new HTTP-level specs covering the three POST routes' validation paths. `/api/file-upload`: invalid JSON → 400; missing required fields → 400; unallowed MIME type → 415; unknown location name → 400 (after MIME-gate). `/api/file-delete`: invalid JSON → 400; missing `uri` → 400; path-traversal denied → 403. `/api/file-rename`: invalid JSON → 400; missing oldUri/newUri → 400; unresolvable oldUri → 403. Route coverage: `delete.js` 0% → 54% lines / 0% → 60% functions; `rename.js` 0% → 53% lines / 60% functions; `upload.js` previously module-load-only, now 33% lines / 33% functions. Aggregate plugin coverage stays at 35% because `dropzone.js` (browser widget, 377 statements, 18% covered) and `startup.js` (218 statements, 27% covered) dominate the line total — both Tier B/D. |
|0.1.28 |2026-05-15 |UI tidy on the delete-confirm modal (same fix as orga-apps 0.2.73 for meeting-delete): move the body's `Cancel` / `Delete anyway` buttons into the modal's `footer:` field so they replace TW core's auto-rendered "Close" fallback (previously the user saw a duplicate `Close` button at the bottom because no `footer:` field was set). ''Drop the body's inline `<$navigator>` wrap'' — it was added in 0.1.21 so the "Delete anyway" button could re-dispatch `tm-delete-tiddler` and have it reach a navigator (appify has none above the modal), but per `tw-modal-inline-navigator-eats-close` that wrap also intercepts the in-modal `tm-close-tiddler` event (NavigatorWidget.handleCloseTiddlerEvent returns `false` unconditionally, breaking widget-event propagation to the modal's body listener) — so both Cancel and Delete-anyway silently failed to close the modal. ''Switch to direct delete'': the new Delete-anyway action calls `$action-deletetiddler $tiddler=<<target>>` instead of re-dispatching `tm-delete-tiddler`. `wiki.deleteTiddler` doesn't invoke the `th-deleting-tiddler` hook (only NavigatorWidget does), so Layer 1 of `startup.js`'s delete handling (the legacy `confirm()` dialog) no longer fires a second prompt after the rich modal — Layer 2's `change`-event listener still fires `cascadeDeleteArtifacts` + `deleteFileFromServer` exactly as before. ''Styling'': the body's `<style scoped>` only reaches the body DOM, not the footer's widget tree, so the `.rr-danger-btn` red styling moved from the scoped block into the plugin's global `styles.tid` |
|0.1.27 |2026-05-15 |''Hotfix for 0.1.26'': tile thumbnails were rendering with `src="{{{"` (or similar literal-text fragments) instead of the actual thumbnail URI. Root cause: when factoring tiles into `fu-att-tile-img` I tried to thread `imgSrc` through as a positional procedure argument via `<<fu-att-tile-img {{{[<imgSrc>]}}}>>`. TW's macro-call argument parser does NOT evaluate `{{{filter}}}` in positional-arg position — it treats it as literal bareword text (and whitespace splits the bareword into more positional args, so `{{{ X }}}` parses as THREE args). The `tw-procedure-call-passes-literal` memory's claim that this works is wrong for positional args (only `<$transclude $variable= attr=<<var>>/>` attribute-syntax actually evaluates). ''Fix'': dropped the params from `fu-att-tile-img` entirely. Each section's `<$let>` now binds `imgSrc` / `showPlayBadge` / `itemCls` in caller scope and the procedure (no params) reads them via inheritance — same pattern that has worked all along for `<<att>>`, `<<fu-att-actions>>`, etc. ''New regression tests'' in `test/test-media-grid.js` actually render the procedures via `wiki.makeWidget(wiki.parseText(...), {}) + render(fakeDoc.createElement)` and assert the `<img src="…">` attribute contains the expected URI for all four tile shapes (PDF thumb, video thumb + play badge, image with thumb, image without thumb), plus EXIF-portrait class application, plus `fu-draggable="yes"` rendering `draggable="true"` on the wrap. These would have caught 0.1.26 immediately if they'd existed |
|0.1.26 |2026-05-15 |''`fu-render-media-grid` grows three opt-in extras'' so consumers no longer need to fork it: (1) ''draggable tiles'' — set `<$let fu-draggable="yes">` and each tile wraps in `<$draggable tiddler=<<att>>>` instead of a plain `<div>`; (2) ''delete-mode dispatch'' — `<$let fu-delete-mode="remove" fu-delete-group=<<group>>>` switches the tile's delete button to `$action-listops $field="members" $subfilter="-[<att>]"` (membership-removal for group views); `fu-delete-mode="none"` hides the button entirely; anything else (default) keeps `tm-delete-tiddler`; (3) ''extra-actions hook'' — new empty default `\procedure fu-att-extra-actions()`; callers redefining it in their own scope get its rendering appended below every tile's action row (used by priv-app for media-group breadcrumb badges). ''EXIF-portrait sizing always-on'' for the image section — reads `exif-width` / `exif-height` / `exif-orientation`, applies new `.fu-att-item-portrait` class (120px wide × 168px-tall thumb) when the photo is taller than wide (accounting for rotated orientations 5/6/7/8); gracefully no-ops when EXIF fields are missing. Internally factored into sub-procedures `fu-att-tile-img(imgSrc, showPlayBadge)`, `fu-att-tile-img-body()`, `fu-att-tile-file()`, `fu-att-tile-file-body()`, `fu-att-delete-button()` so the draggable-or-div wrap is written once. Pairs with priv-app 0.1.15 which deletes `pa-render-media-grid` + `pa-att-actions` entirely and adopts `fu-render-media-grid` for all three media-view variants (group / date / dashboard) — net ~-300 lines in priv-app, single grid implementation in the workspace |
|0.1.25 |2026-05-15 |''`.eml` parents now render Outlook-style in the media-modal'' (matching the existing `.msg` behaviour added in 0.1.23). The modal's body type-switch and footer "Open in new tab" link previously hardcoded `application/vnd.ms-outlook` — clicking an imported `.eml` tile dropped into the fallback "Open file in new tab" branch instead of transcluding the converted `.email` artifact. ''New helper'' `\function fu-att-email-artifact(att)` in `templates/media-grid.tid` returns `<att>.email` for both `application/vnd.ms-outlook` (`.msg`) and `message/rfc822` (`.eml`) parents, empty for everything else. `fu-att-label`, `fu-att-newtab-href`, the modal body branch and the modal footer's open-in-new-tab href all route through this helper now — single point of MIME-list extension if another email format ever shows up. `fu-att-label` gains a `:filter[!is[blank]]` step so an `.email` artifact with an empty `msg-subject` falls back to the filename instead of an empty label. `templates/media-modal.tid` `\import`s `templates/media-grid` so the helper is in scope. ''Test fix'': specs in `test/test-media-grid.js` for `:map`-using filters need a real widget (the `:map` filter prefix calls back into `widget.makeFakeWidgetWithVariables` for each item) — replaced the hand-rolled `{getVariable: ...}` stub with `wiki.makeWidget(wiki.parseText("text/vnd.tiddlywiki", ""), {})` once at describe scope, then `ROOT_WIDGET.makeFakeWidgetWithVariables({att: title})` per spec. 8 new specs: `.eml` → subject, `.eml` missing-`.email` → filename, `.msg` with blank subject → filename, `.eml` newtab href, plus 4 specs pinning `fu-att-email-artifact` dispatch directly |
|0.1.24 |2026-05-14 |Allow `message/rfc822` (.eml) media type and route it to the `email/` subfolder, mirroring the existing `application/vnd.ms-outlook` handling. Pairs with msg-import ≥ 0.1.7, which extends its pipeline + Python extractor to parse `.eml` files via Python's stdlib `email` module (no `extract-msg` dependency for that path) and produces the same `.email` + `.attachments/*` tiddler tree. The dropzone's existing extension-sniff fallback (added in 0.1.20) already maps a bare `.eml` File with no MIME hint to `message/rfc822`, so Thunderbird drag-and-drop is now fully supported end-to-end |
|0.1.23 |2026-05-14 |New ''reusable media-grid + media-modal'' components, so any plugin that lists `_canonical_uri` attachments under a parent gets a uniform UX. `templates/media-grid.tid` exports `fu-render-media-grid(itemFilter)` — a four-section grid (thumbnailed non-image, video with play badge, images, plain files) where each tile has: name (or .msg subject when the .email sibling exists), copy-link, ↗ open-in-new-tab (anchor with `target=_blank` — for `.msg` files this points at the appify permalink `#<.email>` workaround), 🗑 delete (routes through file-upload's existing `tm-delete-tiddler` confirm modal so the cascade is shown), and an inline-popup description editor (✏️ → textarea → Done). `templates/media-modal.tid` exports `fu-media-modal` — overlay that opens on `$:/state/rimir/file-upload/media-modal`; type-switched body renders images via `<img>`, PDFs via `<iframe>`, videos via the existing `fu-render-video-player`, `.msg` via inline-transclude of the `.email` artifact through msg-import's `body/email` (Outlook-style attachments-row + markdown), other types fall back to "Open in new tab" link; footer carries description-textarea + Copy-link + Open-new-tab + Delete buttons. New `styles/media-grid.tid` with all the `.fu-att-*` and `.fu-modal-*` classes. ''Appify-safe by default'': the grid procedure, media-modal procedure AND the existing delete-confirm-modal template each wrap their body in an inline `<$navigator>` with dedicated state tiddlers — appify replaces TW's page navigator, so without this wrap every `tm-delete-tiddler` dispatched from a tile or the modal would silently no-op and file-upload's `handleDeleteTiddlerEvent` patch would never run (see `tw-appify-no-navigator` memory). Sibling navigators with shared state are safe because none of these UIs push to the story (no `tm-navigate`). ''Sub-procedure scope fix'': the modal's `fu-modal-header` / `fu-modal-body` / `fu-modal-footer` originally took an `(att)` parameter and were invoked as `<<fu-modal-body att>>` — but that syntax passes the LITERAL string `"att"` as the parameter value, not the outer `<$let>`'s variable value. Every `[<att>get[type]…]` then resolved against a non-existent tiddler titled `att`, so all four type branches (image / video / pdf / vnd.ms-outlook) missed and the modal always rendered the fallback "Open file in new tab". Fixed by dropping the parameter and letting the sub-procedures inherit `<att>` from the calling `<$let>` scope — matches the pattern priv-app uses for `pa-att-actions`. New memory `tw-procedure-call-passes-literal` documents the gotcha. Drop-in for orga-apps's previously copy-pasted note + meeting attachment grids (consumed by orga-apps ≥ 0.2.66). priv-app's older `pa-render-media-grid` keeps working alongside this — it has extras (media-groups, EXIF-portrait detection) that aren't migrated here. New `test/test-media-grid.js` (10 specs) pins `fu-att-label` (.msg → `.email` msg-subject fallback), `fu-att-newtab-href` (.msg → `#<encoded .email>`, else `_canonical_uri`), and the four `<$list>` section filters' partition behaviour |
|0.1.22 |2026-05-14 |Delete-confirm modal: fixed literal `<$text text=<<target>>/>` rendering — the widget was wrapped in backticks (inline-code), so wikitext skipped widget parsing and showed the raw markup. Quoted the title with `"…"` instead. ''Rejected-upload notification'' — dropzone's MIME allow-list check used to silently drop files with no user feedback; now collects rejections into a `rejected` array (with filename + MIME) and fires a `tm-notify` toast pointing at `$:/plugins/rimir/file-upload/notifications/rejected` after the batch. Result tiddler `$:/temp/file-upload/last-upload` also carries the `rejected` list now. Explains Thunderbird `.eml` drops appearing to do nothing — `message/rfc822` is not in the allow-list (no extractor for it yet); user can see it explicitly instead of guessing |
|0.1.21 |2026-05-14 |Artifact cascade is now ''transitive'' — `cascadeDeleteArtifacts` / `cascadeRenameArtifacts` in `startup.js` walk the `_artifact_source` chain to any depth (BFS for rename, post-order for delete) instead of stopping after one level. Recursive pipelines (PDF attachment of a .msg → PDF thumbnail + extracted text → ...) now cascade-clean properly from the parent. `routes/delete.js`: `deleteDerived` switched to `fs.rmSync(dir, {recursive: true, force: true})` so nested `_derived/<msg>/_derived/<att>/...` chains delete in one call. New `delete-confirm.js` startup module monkey-patches `NavigatorWidget.handleDeleteTiddlerEvent` to open a richer confirmation modal whenever the target tiddler carries `_canonical_uri` (TW's default confirm skips empty-body media tiddlers entirely — easy to lose a PDF + its derived stack to a misclick). The modal lists the full transitive cascade + every backlinking tiddler, with a danger-styled "Delete anyway" button that re-dispatches via a bypass-flag state tiddler. Disable via `$:/config/rimir/file-upload/confirm-deletes` (default `yes`). New helper exports `_deleteDerived`, `_deleteGenerated` on `routes/delete.js` and `_cascadeDeleteArtifacts`, `_cascadeRenameArtifacts`, `_collectCascade`, `_FILE_BACKED_ARTIFACT_TYPES`, `_deleteFileFromServer` on `startup.js` for unit testing. File-backed artifact-type allow-list (`extraction-image`, `attachment`, `derived`, `conversion`, `thumbnail`) means cascade-delete now removes the underlying binary on disk for every file-bearing artifact (previously only `extraction-image`) |
|0.1.20 |2026-05-13 |Allow `application/vnd.ms-outlook` media type, route it to `email/` subfolder. `renameDerived()` in `routes/rename.js`: parent rename now also renames the `_derived/<basename>/` directory (mirrors existing `deleteDerived` in `routes/delete.js`). Benefits file-pipeline pipelines that produce multi-file outputs (PDF images, docx conversions, msg attachments). `dropzone.js`: extension-sniff fallback when `file.type` is empty or `application/octet-stream` (`.msg`→`application/vnd.ms-outlook`, `.eml`→`message/rfc822`). Fixes Outlook drag-and-drop, where Chrome receives a virtual COM file with no MIME hint and the dropzone would otherwise silently skip the file |
|0.1.19 |2026-04-27 |Declare soft-dependents `doc-template`, `file-pipeline` in plugin.info |
|0.1.18 |2026-04-14 |Video body template: inline `<video>` player with thumbnail-first cascade, quality selector (defaults to smallest downscale), resizable wrapper. Shared `fu-render-video-player` procedure. Video metadata extraction via `ffprobe` (date, GPS, dimensions, duration, codec, device). Video EXIF field mapping |
|0.1.17 |2026-04-14 |Binary upload route (`/api/file-upload-binary`): streams raw file to disk, no base64/size limit. Upload progress overlay with percentage. Drag-over highlight CSS. Video subfolder routing (`video/*` → `videos/`). Fix `deleteDerived` for non-default locations + clean empty `_derived/` parent. Replace `magick.exe` with `magick` (native WSL) |
|0.1.16 |2026-04-09 |Pass dropzone `prop-system-prompt`, `prop-provider`, `prop-model` to pipeline client for LLM step overrides |
|0.1.15 |2026-04-09 |file-pipeline integration: `<$file-dropzone>` auto-detects file-pipeline plugin and triggers `pipeline="auto"` on every upload. New `pipeline` attribute ("auto", "<name>", "none"). `upload.js` skips `runProcessor()` when file-pipeline installed. Settings UI shows "configure via file-pipeline" hint for thumbnail settings |
|0.1.14 |2026-04-08 |Fix rename: preserve file directory on rename instead of re-routing by MIME type. Fix thumbnail URI: derive from canonical URI instead of guessing prefix. Use last title segment as filename on rename |
|0.1.13 |2026-04-08 |Add test coverage: uri-resolver, upload/delete/rename route validation, dropzone widget (44→100 jasmine specs) |
|0.1.12 |2026-04-07 |Cleanup: replace \define with \function for thumb-state, replace hardcoded colors with palette variables |
|v0.1.11 |2026-04-07 |Add `target-prefix` attribute to `<$file-dropzone>`: inserts path prefix between subfolder and filename on disk, exposed as variable in action string for tiddler title construction |
|v0.1.10 |2026-04-07 |EXIF extraction: auto-extract metadata from uploaded images via ImageMagick and map to tiddler fields. Configurable global field mapping + per-location overrides. Extracts date, camera, dimensions, GPS, exposure, lens. Enabled by default. |
|v0.1.9 |2026-04-07 |Fix thumbnail cascade: position filter first in ViewTemplateBodyFilter chain (some third-party plugins break cascade evaluation for subsequent filters). Fix draft deletion: skip draft tiddlers in file cleanup to prevent accidental file deletion when cancelling editor. Remove redundant `all[current]` from cascade filter (`:cascade` already provides input title) |
|v0.1.8 |2026-04-07 |Location registry: multi-location support with writable/read-only flag, uri-resolver library, artifact cascade (delete/rename propagates to `_artifact_source` tiddlers), location management UI in settings, `location` attribute on `<$file-dropzone>`, `serve-location` route for user-created locations, optional integration with scattered-binaries and llm-connect |
|v0.1.7 |2026-03-27 |Remove phantom file-paths filter from docs, deduplicate helpers in dropzone.js, bundle default media-types shadow tiddler |
|v0.1.6 |2026-03-15 |Add null guards to th-saving-tiddler and th-renaming-tiddler hooks |
|v0.1.5 |2026-03-15 |Add name field to plugin.info |
|v0.1.4 |2026-03-15 |Add regression tests, CI test gate, and extract helpers library |
|v0.1.3 |2026-03-15 |Fix th-deleting-tiddler hook: return tiddler instead of true to preserve hook chain, add null guard for upstream hooks returning undefined |
|v0.1.2 |2026-03-12 |Add allowed media types section to settings UI, fix missing media-types config causing all uploads to be rejected (415), fix thumbnail generation failing for filenames with spaces (quote paths in processor commands), update dev-workflow docs |
|v0.1.1 |2026-03-06 |Standardize plugin tabs: add documentation/changelog/license to list, replace license.tid with LICENSE.md.meta sidecar |
|v0.1.0 |2026 |Initial release |
